{"kind":"stack","id":"s1","title":"Everyday materials: metals, wood and plastic","theme":{"background":"#f4f7ee","foreground":"#1d2b1a","font":"Georgia, serif"}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"image","picto":"bulb"},{"type":"text","id":"c1-q","content":"Why are metal saucepans used for cooking?"},{"type":"button","id":"c1-a","label":"They conduct heat well","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c1-b","label":"They are always soft and easy to bend","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c1-c","label":"They let light shine through them","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c2","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c2-t","content":"Conductor"},{"type":"text","id":"c2-e","content":"A material that lets heat or electricity pass through it easily. Metals are good conductors."},{"type":"button","id":"c2-n","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c3","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"image","picto":"house"},{"type":"text","id":"c3-q","content":"Why is wood often used to build the frame of a house?"},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a","label":"It is strong and easy to cut and shape","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-b","label":"It melts in the rain","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-c","label":"It is always lighter than air","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-d","label":"It stops all electricity","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c4-q","content":"In a fair test, a pupil drops the same toy car down four ramps made of different materials. What must stay the same?"},{"type":"button","id":"c4-a","label":"The height of the ramp","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-b","label":"The material of the ramp","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-c","label":"The starting height and the car used","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c5-t","content":"Flexible"},{"type":"text","id":"c5-e","content":"A material that bends easily without breaking. Plastic is often flexible, so it can be moulded into bottles."},{"type":"button","id":"c5-n","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c6","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"image","picto":"bulb"},{"type":"text","id":"c6-q","content":"Why are plastic handles often put on metal tools like screwdrivers?"},{"type":"button","id":"c6-a","label":"Plastic is a poor conductor, so it protects the hand from heat and electricity","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c6-b","label":"Plastic makes the tool heavier to use","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c6-c","label":"Plastic makes the metal rust faster","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c7","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c7-t","content":"You are designing a new bridge for a small village. Which material will you choose?"},{"type":"button","id":"c7-a","label":"Steel, because it is strong","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c7-b","label":"Wood, because it is cheap and easy to cut","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c8","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c8-t","content":"Steel is very strong and lasts for years. The village builds a sturdy bridge that carries heavy carts safely."},{"type":"button","id":"c8-n","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c9","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c9-t","content":"Wood is cheap, but it rots when it gets wet. After a few winters the bridge needs repairs."},{"type":"button","id":"c9-n","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c10","kind":"end","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c10-t","content":"Well done! You finished the materials quiz."},{"type":"text","id":"c10-m","content":"Keep testing and asking why materials are chosen for each job."}],"actions":[]}}
